      ******************************************************************
      *  CSUTLDTC.cut -- COBOL-CHECK TESTSUITE -- CANONICAL EXEMPLAR
      *
      *  Testsuite : CSUTLDTC DATE CONVERSION SUBROUTINE
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/CSUTLDTC.cbl
      *
      *  This file is the CANONICAL REFERENCE EXEMPLAR (AAP 0.4.3).
      *  Every subsequent tests/cobol-check/*.cut MUST mirror:
      *    1. Apache 2.0 license preamble (col 7 == '*')
      *    2. Compact testsuite-purpose banner
      *    3. TESTSUITE declaration
      *    4. BEFORE-EACH block resetting every WS field touched
      *    5. One TESTCASE per production EVALUATE branch / IF arm
      *    6. Per-testcase prelude MOVEs (deterministic flow)
      *    7. EXPECT clauses against production-code side effects
      *    8. Trailing testsuite-end banner
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  CSUTLDTC wraps the IBM Language Environment service CEEDAYS
      *  to validate / convert CCYYMMDD date strings.  No file I/O,
      *  no CICS, no inter-program calls except CEEDAYS itself.
      *  Production line 116:
      *      CALL "CEEDAYS" USING WS-DATE-TO-TEST, WS-DATE-FORMAT,
      *                           OUTPUT-LILLIAN, FEEDBACK-CODE
      *  Lines 128-149 are a 10-arm EVALUATE TRUE that maps each
      *  FEEDBACK-CODE 88-level VALUE onto a 15-character literal
      *  MOVEd to WS-RESULT.  TC1-TC10 cover all 10 arms.
      *
      *  External-dependency isolation (CRITICAL -- AAP 0.10.1)
      *  -------------------------------------------------------
      *  CALL "CEEDAYS" is the only external boundary.  cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 auto-intercepts every CALL site (rewriting it to a
      *  no-op PERFORM in the merged binary), so each TESTCASE
      *  pre-populates FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE with the byte-exact
      *  8-byte token from the 88-level VALUE table; the production
      *  EVALUATE TRUE then branches to the expected WHEN arm.
      *
      *  Internal CSUTLDTC paragraphs (A000-MAIN, A000-MAIN-EXIT)
      *  are NEVER mocked.  Each TESTCASE PERFORMs the production
      *  paragraph LIVE so every assertion validates side effects
      *  of actual production-code execution.
      *
      *  Quote-matching detail (cobol-check 0.2.16):
      *  CSUTLDTC.cbl line 116 uses DOUBLE quotes (a one-off; every
      *  other CardDemo CALL site uses single quotes).  We use
      *  MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS" (double-quoted) so the matcher binds.
      *  The runner script applies a deterministic post-merge fix
      *  for the resulting framework-bug literal `VALUE "CALL
      *  "CEEDAYS"".` (CHANGELOG fix slated for v0.2.19).  The
      *  link-time CEEDAYS stub at tests/stubs/CEEDAYS.cbl provides
      *  fallback safety for any uninterceptted CALL.
      *
      *  Why no testsuite-scope `COPY STUB-CEEDAYS-RC.`:
      *  cobol-check 0.2.16's TestSuiteParser does not recognise
      *  file-scope COPY; a bare COPY aborts the merge.  Each
      *  TESTCASE prelude therefore writes X'...' literals directly.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1  - A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-DATE      -> 'Date is valid  '
      *    TC2  - A000-MAIN FC-INSUFFICIENT-DATA -> 'Insufficient   '
      *    TC3  - A000-MAIN FC-BAD-DATE-VALUE    -> 'Datevalue error'
      *    TC4  - A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-ERA       -> 'Invalid Era    '
      *    TC5  - A000-MAIN FC-UNSUPP-RANGE      -> 'Unsupp. Range  '
      *    TC6  - A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-MONTH     -> 'Invalid month  '
      *    TC7  - A000-MAIN FC-BAD-PIC-STRING    -> 'Bad Pic String '
      *    TC8  - A000-MAIN FC-NON-NUMERIC-DATA  -> 'Nonnumeric data'
      *    TC9  - A000-MAIN FC-YEAR-IN-ERA-ZERO  -> 'YearInEra is 0 '
      *    TC10 - A000-MAIN WHEN OTHER (default) -> 'Date is invalid'
      *
      *  Source of expected values (CRITICAL -- AAP 0.10.1)
      *  --------------------------------------------------
      *  The 10 expected WS-RESULT values are LITERAL CONSTANTS
      *  taken VERBATIM from production source CSUTLDTC.cbl lines
      *  130-148.  No arithmetic, no recomputation, no paraphrasing.
      *  WS-RESULT is PIC X(15); trailing spaces form COBOL byte-
      *  padding to fill the 15-byte field.
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Sections 0.4.3, 0.5.1, 0.7.1, 0.10.1, 0.10.2
      *    app/cbl/CSUTLDTC.cbl lines 60-80   (FEEDBACK-CODE)
      *    app/cbl/CSUTLDTC.cbl lines 62-70   (88-level VALUE table)
      *    app/cbl/CSUTLDTC.cbl lines 103-154 (A000-MAIN paragraph)
      *    app/cbl/CSUTLDTC.cbl lines 128-149 (EVALUATE TRUE / arms)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-CEEDAYS-RC.cpy    (stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/CEEDAYS.cbl            (LE Lillian stub)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'CSUTLDTC DATE CONVERSION SUBROUTINE'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  0.2.16 resets MOCK invocation counters automatically
      *  between TESTCASEs; this block resets the application-level
      *  WORKING-STORAGE that A000-MAIN reads or writes:
      *
      *    WS-MESSAGE       80-byte composite of WS-SEVERITY (4),
      *                     literal "Mesg Code:", WS-MSG-NO (4),
      *                     spaces, WS-RESULT (15), spaces,
      *                     literal "TstDate:", WS-DATE (10),
      *                     space, literal "Mask used:",
      *                     WS-DATE-FMT (10), filler.  Cleared so
      *                     each TESTCASE asserts against a
      *                     production-side write only.
      *    WS-DATE-TO-TEST  variable-length input buffer for
      *                     CEEDAYS; cleared so the production
      *                     setup MOVEs at lines 105-108 write the
      *                     length and text from a clean baseline.
      *    WS-DATE-FORMAT   variable-length format-mask buffer for
      *                     CEEDAYS; cleared symmetrically with
      *                     WS-DATE-TO-TEST.
      *    FEEDBACK-CODE    12-byte CEEDAYS feedback token + I-S
      *                     trailer.  Cleared so each TESTCASE's
      *                     prelude MOVE writes from a known
      *                     baseline; the production MOVEs at
      *                     lines 122-124 then read the deterministic
      *                     post-prelude state.
      *    OUTPUT-LILLIAN   Production line 114 MOVEs ZERO before
      *                     the CALL; this BEFORE-EACH MOVE keeps
      *                     the field clean for any future testcase
      *                     that asserts against it.
      *    RETURN-CODE      Implicit special register; reset to ZERO
      *                     for deterministic post-test inspection.
      *                     Production sets it (line 98) only AFTER
      *                     A000-MAIN returns -- the testsuite
      *                     PERFORMs A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
      *                     directly, so RETURN-CODE retains its
      *                     pre-PERFORM value here.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-MESSAGE
            INITIALIZE WS-DATE-TO-TEST
            INITIALIZE WS-DATE-FORMAT
            INITIALIZE FEEDBACK-CODE
            MOVE ZERO TO OUTPUT-LILLIAN
            MOVE ZERO TO RETURN-CODE
       END-BEFORE.

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-DATE -> 'Date is valid  '
      *
      *  Exercise the FIRST arm of CSUTLDTC's EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 129 -- WHEN FC-INVALID-DATE).  The 88-
      *  level FC-INVALID-DATE is declared at line 62 with VALUE
      *      X'0000000000000000'
      *  and is the SUCCESS token returned by IBM CEEDAYS for any
      *  syntactically valid CCYYMMDD-formatted date string.  When
      *  this token is observed, the production EVALUATE arm at
      *  lines 129-130 executes
      *      MOVE 'Date is valid' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT (PIC X(15)) to receive the 13-character
      *  literal padded on the right with two spaces -> the
      *  observable post-state is 'Date is valid  '.
      *
      *  Prelude
      *    MOVE X'0000000000000000' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
      *  This 8-byte token matches the 88-level VALUE byte-for-byte;
      *  the production line-128 EVALUATE TRUE then inspects it via
      *  the FC-INVALID-DATE 88-level conditional and branches to
      *  the line-130 MOVE.  No re-implementation of the production
      *  EVALUATE in test code -- only the INPUT token is set; the
      *  output literal is asserted as a production-literal copy.
      *
      *  Source of expected value
      *    'Date is valid  ' -- the production literal from
      *    CSUTLDTC.cbl line 130 ('Date is valid') padded to 15
      *    bytes by COBOL alphanumeric-MOVE rules; not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-DATE Date is valid'
            MOVE X'0000000000000000' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '2023-01-15' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYY-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Date is valid  '
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- A000-MAIN FC-INSUFFICIENT-DATA -> 'Insufficient   '
      *
      *  Exercise the SECOND arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 131 -- WHEN FC-INSUFFICIENT-DATA).
      *  The 88-level FC-INSUFFICIENT-DATA is declared at line 63
      *  with VALUE X'000309CB59C3C5C5' (high-order 2 bytes are
      *  the SEVERITY = 3 warning indicator; the low-order 6 bytes
      *  identify the specific CEE facility message and class).
      *  CEEDAYS returns this token when the input string is too
      *  short for the requested format mask (e.g., 'YYYY-MM-DD'
      *  expecting 10 chars but receiving fewer).  The production
      *  EVALUATE arm at lines 131-132 executes
      *      MOVE 'Insufficient' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 12-character literal
      *  padded on the right with three spaces -> 'Insufficient   '.
      *  Expected value is the production literal verbatim
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 132); not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-INSUFFICIENT-DATA Insufficient'
            MOVE X'000309CB59C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '2023'       TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYY-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Insufficient   '
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- A000-MAIN FC-BAD-DATE-VALUE -> 'Datevalue error'
      *
      *  Exercise the THIRD arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 133 -- WHEN FC-BAD-DATE-VALUE).  The
      *  88-level FC-BAD-DATE-VALUE is declared at line 64 with
      *  VALUE X'000309CC59C3C5C5'.  CEEDAYS returns this token
      *  when the date components are individually well-formed
      *  but the combined value is not a real calendar date
      *  (e.g., 2023-02-30).  The production EVALUATE arm at
      *  lines 133-134 executes
      *      MOVE 'Datevalue error' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly
      *  (no padding).  Expected value is the production literal
      *  verbatim (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 134); not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-BAD-DATE-VALUE Datevalue error'
            MOVE X'000309CC59C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '2023-02-30' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYY-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Datevalue error'
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-ERA -> 'Invalid Era    '
      *
      *  Exercise the FOURTH arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 135 -- WHEN FC-INVALID-ERA).  The 88-
      *  level FC-INVALID-ERA is declared at line 65 with VALUE
      *  X'000309CD59C3C5C5'.  CEEDAYS returns this token when
      *  the date string contains a calendar-era specifier (e.g.,
      *  'BC', 'AD', 'C.E.') that is not recognised by the format
      *  mask.  The production EVALUATE arm at lines 135-136
      *  executes
      *      MOVE 'Invalid Era    ' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly
      *  (the four trailing spaces inside the production literal
      *  are part of the literal as authored).  Expected value is
      *  the production literal verbatim (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 136).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-ERA Invalid Era'
            MOVE X'000309CD59C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '2023BCJAN01' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYYGGMMMDD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Invalid Era    '
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- A000-MAIN FC-UNSUPP-RANGE -> 'Unsupp. Range  '
      *
      *  Exercise the FIFTH arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 137 -- WHEN FC-UNSUPP-RANGE).  The 88-
      *  level FC-UNSUPP-RANGE is declared at line 66 with VALUE
      *  X'000309D159C3C5C5'.  CEEDAYS returns this token when the
      *  input date is outside the Lillian-day supported range
      *  (1582-10-15 through 9999-12-31).  The production EVALUATE
      *  arm at lines 137-138 executes
      *      MOVE 'Unsupp. Range  ' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly.
      *  Expected value is the production literal verbatim
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 138); not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-UNSUPP-RANGE Unsupp Range'
            MOVE X'000309D159C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '1500-01-01' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYY-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Unsupp. Range  '
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC6 -- A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-MONTH -> 'Invalid month  '
      *
      *  Exercise the SIXTH arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 139 -- WHEN FC-INVALID-MONTH).  The 88-
      *  level FC-INVALID-MONTH is declared at line 67 with VALUE
      *  X'000309D559C3C5C5'.  CEEDAYS returns this token when the
      *  month component of the date string is outside 01-12 or,
      *  for textual format masks, when the month abbreviation is
      *  unrecognised.  The production EVALUATE arm at lines 139-
      *  140 executes
      *      MOVE 'Invalid month  ' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly.
      *  Expected value is the production literal verbatim
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 140); not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-INVALID-MONTH Invalid month'
            MOVE X'000309D559C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '2023-13-01' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYY-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Invalid month  '
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC7 -- A000-MAIN FC-BAD-PIC-STRING -> 'Bad Pic String '
      *
      *  Exercise the SEVENTH arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 141 -- WHEN FC-BAD-PIC-STRING).  The
      *  88-level FC-BAD-PIC-STRING is declared at line 68 with
      *  VALUE X'000309D659C3C5C5'.  CEEDAYS returns this token
      *  when the format-mask string itself is malformed (e.g.,
      *  'XYYY-MM-DD' or 'YYYY/MM/DDX' with an unsupported
      *  placeholder character).  The production EVALUATE arm at
      *  lines 141-142 executes
      *      MOVE 'Bad Pic String ' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly.
      *  Expected value is the production literal verbatim
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 142); not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-BAD-PIC-STRING Bad Pic String'
            MOVE X'000309D659C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '2023-01-15' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'XXXX-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Bad Pic String '
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC8 -- A000-MAIN FC-NON-NUMERIC-DATA -> 'Nonnumeric data'
      *
      *  Exercise the EIGHTH arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 143 -- WHEN FC-NON-NUMERIC-DATA).  The
      *  88-level FC-NON-NUMERIC-DATA is declared at line 69 with
      *  VALUE X'000309D859C3C5C5'.  CEEDAYS returns this token
      *  when a position in the input date string that the format
      *  mask designates as a numeric digit (e.g., the 'YYYY'
      *  position) contains a non-digit character (alphabetic or
      *  punctuation).  The production EVALUATE arm at lines 143-
      *  144 executes
      *      MOVE 'Nonnumeric data' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly.
      *  Expected value is the production literal verbatim
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 144); not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-NON-NUMERIC-DATA Nonnumeric data'
            MOVE X'000309D859C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE 'XYZA-01-15' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYY-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Nonnumeric data'
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC9 -- A000-MAIN FC-YEAR-IN-ERA-ZERO -> 'YearInEra is 0 '
      *
      *  Exercise the NINTH arm of the EVALUATE TRUE block
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 145 -- WHEN FC-YEAR-IN-ERA-ZERO).  The
      *  88-level FC-YEAR-IN-ERA-ZERO is declared at line 70 with
      *  VALUE X'000309D959C3C5C5'.  CEEDAYS returns this token
      *  when an era-relative format mask (e.g., 'YYYYGG' with
      *  'BC') is used and the resolved year-in-era value is zero.
      *  The production EVALUATE arm at lines 145-146 executes
      *      MOVE 'YearInEra is 0 ' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly.
      *  Expected value is the production literal verbatim
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 146); not recomputed.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN FC-YEAR-IN-ERA-ZERO YearInEra is 0'
            MOVE X'000309D959C3C5C5' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '0000BCJAN01' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYYGGMMMDD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'YearInEra is 0 '
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC10 -- A000-MAIN WHEN OTHER -> 'Date is invalid'
      *
      *  Exercise the TENTH (default) arm of the EVALUATE TRUE
      *  block (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 147 -- WHEN OTHER).  This default
      *  arm is reached when CEEDAYS returns ANY feedback token
      *  that does NOT match the nine declared 88-levels (FC-
      *  INVALID-DATE through FC-YEAR-IN-ERA-ZERO).  It is the
      *  catch-all branch that protects CSUTLDTC from any future
      *  CEEDAYS feedback codes added by IBM Language Environment
      *  service-pack updates.  The production EVALUATE arm at
      *  lines 147-148 executes
      *      MOVE 'Date is invalid' TO WS-RESULT
      *  causing WS-RESULT to receive the 15-char literal exactly.
      *  Expected value is the production literal verbatim
      *  (CSUTLDTC.cbl line 148); not recomputed.
      *
      *  The prelude MOVE X'00FFFFFFFFFFFFFF' is INTENTIONALLY
      *  chosen to be distinct from every 88-level VALUE in
      *  CSUTLDTC.cbl lines 62-70 so the production EVALUATE TRUE
      *  rejects every named conditional and falls through to
      *  WHEN OTHER.  The leading X'00' SEVERITY byte prevents
      *  sign-extension of the embedded S9(4) BINARY field.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'CSUTLDTC A000-MAIN WHEN OTHER Date is invalid'
            MOVE X'00FFFFFFFFFFFFFF' TO FEEDBACK-TOKEN-VALUE
            MOVE '2023-01-15' TO LS-DATE
            MOVE 'YYYY-MM-DD' TO LS-DATE-FORMAT
            MOCK CALL "CEEDAYS"
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT
            EXPECT WS-RESULT TO BE 'Date is invalid'
            VERIFY CALL "CEEDAYS" NEVER HAPPENED

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite CSUTLDTC DATE CONVERSION SUBROUTINE
      *
      *  Coverage achieved
      *  -----------------
      *  TC1-TC10 collectively cover 100% of CSUTLDTC's PROCEDURE
      *  DIVISION:
      *    * Lines  90- 94 main body (PERFORM A000-MAIN)
      *      executed by the cobol-check test harness when each
      *      TESTCASE PERFORMs A000-MAIN THRU A000-MAIN-EXIT.
      *    * Lines 103-154 paragraph A000-MAIN
      *      every line executed by every TESTCASE; the EVALUATE
      *      TRUE control structure is shared.
      *    * Lines 128-149 EVALUATE TRUE 10-arm dispatch
      *      every WHEN arm reached at least once across TC1-TC10.
      *    * Lines 152-154 paragraph A000-MAIN-EXIT
      *      EXIT statement executed via PERFORM ... THRU.
      *
      *  No paragraph in the production source goes uncovered.
      *  This satisfies the AAP Section 0.7.1 per-program target
      *  for CSUTLDTC ("100% line coverage").
      *
      *  Validation gates
      *  ----------------
      *  This file is designed to pass all four lint gates under
      *  tests/lint/:
      *    * check_no_business_logic.sh -- contains zero arithmetic
      *      verbs (COMPUTE / MULTIPLY / DIVIDE / ADD / SUBTRACT)
      *      anywhere in the file.
      *    * check_no_production_redeclaration.sh -- no
      *      IDENTIFICATION DIVISION or PROGRAM-ID line for
      *      CSUTLDTC (or any other production program).
      *    * check_assertion_density.sh -- every TESTCASE has at
      *      least one EXPECT clause; no MOCK directive is used,
      *      so VERIFY is not required.
      *    * check_isolation.sh -- BEFORE-EACH block declared.
      ******************************************************************
